    "updated_at": "2026-10-24T17:29:21Z",
    "body": "I always found this to be a weird part of the specification... Is it really the *byte source*'s fault that the BYOB reader is trying to do a multi-byte `read(view)`, but there just aren't any more bytes? 🤔\n\nI'm wondering if we should just get rid of the [\"throw _e_\" in step 4.2.3 of `ReadableByteStreamControllerClose`](https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/#readable-byte-stream-controller-close), and let the byte source tear down \"normally\" while only the reader gets the error.",
